;; Same task as work-kotoba-delta.edn, but the fleet requires a human sign-off
;; before anything that touches `test/` may materialize.
;;
;; :protected-paths are refused outright; :signoff-paths are allowed but only
;; behind a signed approval from an enrolled DID — the difference between "an
;; agent may never do this" and "a human decides this one".
{:work-id "kd-signoff-demo"
 :unit    "kotoba-lang/kotoba-delta#signoff"
 :repo    "kotoba-lang/kotoba-delta"
 :pin     "c8c405abda731e5889aff3ae2a18ac208b375bb5"
 :node    "naphtali"
 :requires #{:nbb :git}
 :test-cmd "kbb --backend sci --classpath src:test run-tests.cljs"
 :ttl-ms  1800000
 :protected-paths [".github/" ".git/" "package.json"]
 :signoff-paths ["test/"]
 :budget  {:max-turns 12 :max-tool-calls 30 :max-tokens 4000
           :deadline-ms 1200000 :test-timeout-ms 180000}
 :prompt
 "Task: add one small pure helper to this repository, with a test.

  1. In src/delta/op.cljc add a function `ops-for-file`:
     (defn ops-for-file [ops file] ...) — returns, in log order, the ops in
     `ops` whose :op/file equals `file`. Give it a short docstring. It must be
     pure and must not change any existing function.
  2. In test/delta/op_test.cljc add a deftest named `ops-for-file-filters`
     asserting that a known file yields only that file's ops in order, and an
     unknown file yields an empty result.
  3. Run the tests and make sure they pass.

  Touch only those two files."}
